1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,239
Users Change Email is an Orchard Core feature that lets each signed-in user

2
00:00:05,239 --> 00:00:07,960
change the email address of their own account.

3
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:11,570
In this video, you enable it, turn on its setting, and follow a

4
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:13,140
user through the change.

5
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:22,955
By default, the Email field on the edit page of an existing user can't be edited.

6
00:00:22,955 --> 00:00:28,830
The User Login setting, Allow user to change their email address, makes that field editable.

7
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:32,886
The Users Change Email feature adds another way:

8
00:00:32,886 --> 00:00:36,681
a Change Email item in the user menu, and a page where a

9
00:00:36,681 --> 00:00:39,559
signed-in user types a different address.

10
00:00:39,559 --> 00:00:42,130
A site setting turns both on or off.

11
00:00:46,322 --> 00:00:48,869
This is the Features page, under Tools.

12
00:00:48,869 --> 00:00:50,906
Let's search for change email.

13
00:00:50,906 --> 00:00:55,942
The feature is called Users Change Email, and it's listed in the Security category.

14
00:00:56,396 --> 00:00:57,609
Select Enable.

15
00:00:57,609 --> 00:01:02,036
A message confirms that the feature Users Change Email was enabled.

16
00:01:06,235 --> 00:01:09,115
This is Settings, Security, Change Email.

17
00:01:09,115 --> 00:01:11,566
Enabling the feature isn't enough:

18
00:01:11,566 --> 00:01:15,917
until the setting is on, the user menu doesn't show the item, and

19
00:01:15,917 --> 00:01:18,735
the Change Email page returns not found.

20
00:01:19,191 --> 00:01:23,014
Check Allow the users to change their email, and select Save.

21
00:01:23,014 --> 00:01:25,981
The setting applies to every user of the site.

22
00:01:26,449 --> 00:01:28,047
A message confirms it:

23
00:01:28,047 --> 00:01:30,387
Site settings updated successfully.

24
00:01:30,387 --> 00:01:35,809
Clearing the checkbox hides the item and the page again, while the feature stays enabled.

25
00:01:40,109 --> 00:01:43,145
This is the Users list, under Access Control.

26
00:01:43,145 --> 00:01:46,360
Any signed-in user can change their own address.

27
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:50,289
In the admin, the user menu is the user icon in the top bar.

28
00:01:50,770 --> 00:01:54,590
The menu starts with Signed in as, followed by the user name.

29
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:58,296
Change Email is listed between Change password and Log off.

30
00:01:58,296 --> 00:01:59,550
Let's select it.

31
00:02:00,015 --> 00:02:05,233
The Change Email page has one field, Email, filled with the current address of the account.

32
00:02:05,233 --> 00:02:07,815
Let's replace it with a different address.

33
00:02:08,285 --> 00:02:09,403
Select Submit.

34
00:02:09,403 --> 00:02:11,919
The Email changed page thanks the user.

35
00:02:11,919 --> 00:02:15,273
The address is saved as soon as the form is submitted:

36
00:02:15,273 --> 00:02:19,298
the form asks for the address only, and the module doesn't ask the

37
00:02:19,298 --> 00:02:20,695
user to confirm it.

38
00:02:21,156 --> 00:02:25,185
Back on the Users list, the row of the user shows the replacement

39
00:02:25,185 --> 00:02:27,228
address next to the user name.

40
00:02:27,228 --> 00:02:32,506
At sign-in, the user can also type that address in the Username or email address field.

41
00:02:36,732 --> 00:02:39,527
The page checks an address before it saves it.

42
00:02:39,527 --> 00:02:43,503
If the address is the one the account already has, the page answers:

43
00:02:43,503 --> 00:02:45,922
This email is already your current one.

44
00:02:46,382 --> 00:02:50,348
If another user already has the address, the page answers:

45
00:02:50,348 --> 00:02:53,322
A user with the same email already exists.

46
00:02:53,776 --> 00:02:58,221
A value that isn't an email address is refused with a validation message.

47
00:02:58,221 --> 00:03:01,766
In each case, the address of the account stays as it was.

48
00:03:05,966 --> 00:03:06,860
To sum up:

49
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:11,944
enable the feature, turn on the setting, and users choose Change Email in their menu.

50
00:03:11,944 --> 00:03:18,256
When the Deployment feature is enabled, a deployment step called Change Email settings exports the setting.

51
00:03:20,256 --> 00:03:21,940
That's Users Change Email:

52
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:25,517
a menu item and a page that let signed-in users keep their own

53
00:03:25,517 --> 00:03:27,148
email address up to date.

54
00:03:27,148 --> 00:03:28,516
Thanks for watching.

